WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.090
Picture two made-up
animals of similar size,

2
00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.920
resting in a chamber.

3
00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.500
The air is 10 degrees Celsius.

4
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.150
Animal X's body stays near 38 degrees.

5
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.880
Animal Y's is close to
the air, at about 11.

6
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.310
Warm the air to 30 degrees.

7
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.220
X barely changes.

8
00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.480
Y warms with the air.

9
00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:25.650
Your own core temperature
barely moves in snow or in sun.

10
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.960
How does your body manage
that, and at what cost?

11
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:33.080
In this mission, you'll compare animals
that hold their temperature steady with

12
00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.550
animals that follow their surroundings.

13
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.630
Then you'll see what a body
does when it gets too hot,

14
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.170
or too cold.

15
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:44.670
Your mission: explain how your body
holds its core temperature steady,

16
00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.110
and what that costs.
